WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:06.450
“Good grief,” said Jotaro Kujo as he,
his grandfather Joseph Joestar, and the rest

00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:11.030
of their allied group of stand users hid from
the light of day in the shadows of a ruined

00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:12.030
building.

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:17.510
Outside, amorphous semi-humanoid monstrosities
roamed free in search of life.

00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:18.850
How could this have happened?

00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:23.410
Jotaro’s family had been on some bizarre
adventures, but this one was proving to be

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:25.560
the most bizarre of all.

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:32.840
The Sun, now designated SCP-001, was burning
with intense bright red light and an anomalous

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:34.160
level of heat.

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:38.550
It beat down on the world below like an evil
and sadistic god of the desert.

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:43.610
The entire world was at the mercy of these
oppressive solar rays, and high temperatures

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:45.440
were just the beginning.

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:51.020
From the looks of it, any living thing exposed
to the rays of SCP-001 would quickly dissolve

00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:56.109
into a horrible gooey substance that would
ooze towards other organisms in an attempt

00:00:56.109 --> 00:00:58.920
to absorb them into its biomass.

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:03.980
Basically, it was like a zombie apocalypse
straight out of an easy bake oven.

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:08.650
The Stardust Crusaders had been passing through
this city on their globe-trotting adventure,

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:12.500
only to find that morning had brought with
it a disaster the likes of which had never

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:14.060
been seen before.

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:18.520
By mid-afternoon, when the sun was highest
in the sky, most of the people had already

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:24.030
been converted into slime monsters, and those
who fled into the shadows found themselves

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:27.390
relentlessly hunted down and absorbed.

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:31.640
Only the stand users of Jotaro’s group,
who were already on the lookout for strange

00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:35.710
happenings, had been clever enough to pick
up on the situation immediately.

00:01:35.710 --> 00:01:40.159
They had been the subject of many unusual
supernatural attacks over the course of their

00:01:40.159 --> 00:01:45.180
journey, so the initial anomalous effects
of SCP-001 seemed to be another routine brush

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:46.180
with an enemy.

00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:47.180
“Hey, Jotaro!

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:50.140
This has to be the effect of an enemy stand,
right?”

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:51.140
Joseph said.

00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:52.140
“What?

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:53.889
Are you stupid or something, old man?”

00:01:53.889 --> 00:01:55.860
spat Jean Pierre Polnareff.

00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:59.729
The Frenchman was ever the impulsive one,
and he always found something to complain

00:01:59.729 --> 00:02:01.920
about when a woman wasn’t present.

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:05.049
He was selectively polite, one might say.

00:02:05.049 --> 00:02:09.940
It was fitting given the fact that his stand,
Silver Chariot, took the form of a sword-wielding

00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:14.520
knight and its reaction speed was the fastest
of any of the Stardust Crusaders.

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:17.590
“You think one Stand could do all this?”

00:02:17.590 --> 00:02:19.550
Polnareff was adamant about making his point.

00:02:19.550 --> 00:02:24.910
Jotaro’s fellow high school classmate Noriaki
Kakyoin was the next to speak.

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:26.489
“Polnareff, keep your voice down.

00:02:26.489 --> 00:02:30.300
We can’t be sure it's not a stand, but either
way, those flesh monsters are looking for

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:31.300
us.”

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:35.660
Kakyoin was younger than Polnareff, but tended
to carry himself with more composure.

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:39.610
This likely had something to do with the fact
that Hierophant Green was the group’s most

00:02:39.610 --> 00:02:42.250
technical stand and often used for reconnaissance.

00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:44.270
“What do you think, Avdol?”

00:02:44.270 --> 00:02:45.270
Kakyoin continued.

00:02:45.270 --> 00:02:46.760
“You’re the expert here.”

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:51.900
Muhammad Avdol, a fortune teller who possessed
a stand that controls fire - Magician’s

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:54.470
Red - was often knowledgable about the supernatural.

00:02:54.470 --> 00:02:58.379
“A stand this powerful would have to be
limited in the range it could affect.”

00:02:58.379 --> 00:02:59.379
Avdol said.

00:02:59.379 --> 00:03:03.599
“What we have to do is get further away
from this area, then we’ll see if this strange

00:03:03.599 --> 00:03:04.599
sunlight fades.”

00:03:04.599 --> 00:03:07.159
“But what if the user is following us?”

00:03:07.159 --> 00:03:08.159
Joseph interjected.

00:03:08.159 --> 00:03:11.150
“How will we know we aren’t putting more
people at risk?”

00:03:11.150 --> 00:03:15.890
“Mr. Joestar, we can’t win this battle
without more information,” Avdol replied.

00:03:15.890 --> 00:03:19.280
“Kakyoin, your Hierophant Green has the
longest range.

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:21.900
Send it to scout for a place outside of this
stand’s reach.

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:26.120
Our stands shouldn’t be visible to those
transformed humans, and the heat from sunlight

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:28.250
won’t affect something without mass.”

00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:32.590
Friendly reminder to those of you at home
unfamiliar with the properties of Stands.

00:03:32.590 --> 00:03:37.630
Stands are spectral entities formed from the
soul of the user, and are essentially superpowered

00:03:37.630 --> 00:03:40.150
ghosts without physical presence.

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:45.010
As such, they wouldn’t be affected by SCP-001
the way a living thing would.

00:03:45.010 --> 00:03:47.110
Now back to this bizarre adventure.

00:03:47.110 --> 00:03:48.110
“Right.”

00:03:48.110 --> 00:03:49.110
Kakyoin nodded.

00:03:49.110 --> 00:03:50.430
“Hierophant Green!”

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:54.910
Kakyoin summoned his stand and began threading
Hierophant Green’s long, stretchy body throughout

00:03:54.910 --> 00:03:57.209
the ruins as far as it could go.

00:03:57.209 --> 00:04:01.180
The young man concentrated, looking through
the eyes of his stand.

00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:06.900
As Kakyoin and his stand searched for the
end of the anomalous effects of SCP-001, Polnareff

00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:09.010
continued to complain as usual.

00:04:09.010 --> 00:04:13.360
“So we’re still not sure what is going
on, but from what I’ve heard, you’re already

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:14.580
calling it a stand?

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:16.680
Did I get that right, Avdol?”

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:17.680
Polnareff grumbled.

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:19.709
“Do you have any better ideas, Polnareff?”

00:04:19.709 --> 00:04:21.250
Avdol said sternly.

00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:22.250
“Iggy!”

00:04:22.250 --> 00:04:25.190
barked Iggy, the last member of the stardust
crusaders.

00:04:25.190 --> 00:04:30.250
He was a Boston terrier who commanded a sand-manipulating
stand known as The Fool.

00:04:30.250 --> 00:04:34.820
Iggy didn’t really have much to add to the
conversation, but he liked to be heard.

00:04:34.820 --> 00:04:36.730
“Listen…” said Joseph Joestar.

00:04:36.730 --> 00:04:41.510
“When I was a younger man, I actually did
go head-to-head with some terrifying beings

00:04:41.510 --> 00:04:46.031
who might be able to turn people into monsters
like those, but every single time the sun

00:04:46.031 --> 00:04:47.850
was the enemy of those guys.”

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:53.669
“Nobody is interested in hearing your stories
right now, old man,” Jotaro chided his grandfather.

00:04:53.669 --> 00:04:58.550
Meanwhile, far from where the Stardust Crusaders
were hiding out, Hierophant Green was reaching

00:04:58.550 --> 00:05:04.280
the limits of its effective range and seeing
no sign of an end to the anomalous effects.

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:05.750
Kakyoin was baffled.

00:05:05.750 --> 00:05:09.410
Could it be true that the entire world had
been affected by the frightening ability of

00:05:09.410 --> 00:05:13.130
the sun now that it was SCP-001?

00:05:13.130 --> 00:05:18.420
If that was true then this apocalyptic wasteland
was more than just the work of an enemy stand

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:19.530
user.

00:05:19.530 --> 00:05:23.870
This would mean that the sun itself had become
the enemy of all life.

00:05:23.870 --> 00:05:28.660
Kakyoin wondered about his family back in
Japan: would they manage to survive this terrible

00:05:28.660 --> 00:05:29.660
catastrophe?

00:05:29.660 --> 00:05:34.449
He couldn’t help but hope that there was
some way out of this utter devastation, even

00:05:34.449 --> 00:05:38.650
though the information gathered by his stand
told him otherwise.

00:05:38.650 --> 00:05:42.470
Kakyoin withdrew Hierophant Green and brought
his companions up to speed.

00:05:42.470 --> 00:05:47.940
However hard it was to accept, the world as
they knew it was gone with the daybreak.

00:05:47.940 --> 00:05:53.590
Polnareff was beside himself in sadness, while
Avdol and Joseph exchanged a meaningful glance.

00:05:53.590 --> 00:05:58.380
For once, Iggy’s bad attitude subsided,
and the dog simply whimpered.

00:05:58.380 --> 00:06:00.900
Only Jotaro remained determined to carry on.

00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:03.819
“Good grief, would all of you get a hold
of yourselves?”

00:06:03.819 --> 00:06:04.819
Jotaro said.

00:06:04.819 --> 00:06:08.949
“We’ll remain human as long as we aren't
caught in that light, so I’ll use Star Platinum

00:06:08.949 --> 00:06:11.050
to tunnel our way underground.”

00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:16.009
Jotaro’s Star Platinum was a short-range
stand, but in terms of raw power it was off

00:06:16.009 --> 00:06:17.009
the charts.

00:06:17.009 --> 00:06:21.949
Its punches could easily tunnel through solid
rock and create a subterranean passageway

00:06:21.949 --> 00:06:24.790
for the Crusaders to retreat to a safer area.

00:06:24.790 --> 00:06:26.240
“Thattaboy, Jotaro!”

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:27.300
Joseph exclaimed.

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:29.410
“We’ll make our daring escape, mole-style!

00:06:29.410 --> 00:06:30.410
”

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:33.050
Jotaro nodded and called Star Platinum.

00:06:33.050 --> 00:06:36.370
Shouting its signature battle cry of “ora
ora!!”

00:06:36.370 --> 00:06:41.430
Star Platinum smashed through the earth below,
instantly creating the entrance to a tunnel.

00:06:41.430 --> 00:06:46.080
At that exact moment, every flesh monster
in the nearby vicinity turned its attention

00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:47.610
towards the sound.

00:06:47.610 --> 00:06:52.289
The stand users had to move quickly, because
they would soon be completely surrounded.

00:06:52.289 --> 00:06:54.690
“OH MY GOD!!!”

00:06:54.690 --> 00:06:59.680
shouted Joseph in his usual way, as a couple
of flesh monsters began to enter the ruined

00:06:59.680 --> 00:07:00.680
building.

00:07:00.680 --> 00:07:05.950
Luckily, Polnareff and Avdol sprung into action
and summoned Silver Chariot and Magician’s

00:07:05.950 --> 00:07:08.860
Red to fend off the flesh zombies.

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:14.099
Silver Chariot delivered an inescapably fast
flurry of sword strikes to one of the monsters,

00:07:14.099 --> 00:07:18.410
while Magician’s Red burned them away with
its supernatural flames.

00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:21.229
The two men high-fived at a job well done.

00:07:21.229 --> 00:07:26.460
Just then, the wall next to them burst open,
revealing a new monster and causing the sun’s

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:29.330
rays to enter into the building’s interior.

00:07:29.330 --> 00:07:33.849
With split-second intuition, Avdol pushed
Polnareff further into the shadows.

00:07:33.849 --> 00:07:38.970
The Frenchman tumbled backwards into the hole
Jotaro made, and before he could get his bearings,

00:07:38.970 --> 00:07:43.070
he caught a glimpse of Avdol being absorbed
into the monster’s mass.

00:07:43.070 --> 00:07:44.070
“AVDOL!”

00:07:44.070 --> 00:07:45.070
He cried out.

00:07:45.070 --> 00:07:50.120
But it was too late, Avdol was already starting
to show signs of transformation into an ooze-like

00:07:50.120 --> 00:07:51.760
zombie himself.

00:07:51.760 --> 00:07:56.960
The fortune teller breathed in deep, and called
the name of his stand with determined fervor.

00:07:56.960 --> 00:07:58.560
“Magician’s Red!”

00:07:58.560 --> 00:08:02.949
Before Avdol could fully be taken by the slime,
he unleashed the totality of his fire power

00:08:02.949 --> 00:08:08.430
on every zombified lifeform within range,
its destructive heat enhanced by the dryness

00:08:08.430 --> 00:08:09.780
of the atmosphere.

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:14.610
Avdol turned back to his friends and gave
them a heartful thumbs up before he disappeared

00:08:14.610 --> 00:08:16.360
into the flames.

00:08:16.360 --> 00:08:20.599
Polnareff cried out for his friend again,
with tears in his eyes, but Kakyoin and Joseph

00:08:20.599 --> 00:08:24.199
grabbed him and made their way deeper into
the tunnel.

00:08:24.199 --> 00:08:28.789
As badass and heroic as it was, Avdol’s
sacrifice wouldn’t keep those hordes of

00:08:28.789 --> 00:08:30.750
monsters at bay for long.

00:08:30.750 --> 00:08:35.690
While Kaykoin and Joseph dragged a crying
Polnareff through the underground escape route,

00:08:35.690 --> 00:08:39.570
Jotaro and Iggy were already at the front
of the group, using a combination of Star

00:08:39.570 --> 00:08:44.540
Platinum’s digging ability and Iggy’s
sand manipulation to stabilize the tunnel.

00:08:44.540 --> 00:08:48.720
The Stardust Crusaders were deep beneath the
surface of the earth now, so a cave-in could

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:49.920
be a real problem.

00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:51.870
“We have to go back!!”

00:08:51.870 --> 00:08:52.870
Polnareff shrieked.

00:08:52.870 --> 00:08:54.290
“Avdol needs our help!”

00:08:54.290 --> 00:08:56.010
“It’s too late, Polnareff.”

00:08:56.010 --> 00:08:57.600
Joseph said, with grim conviction.

00:08:57.600 --> 00:08:58.980
“Avdol is gone.”

00:08:58.980 --> 00:09:01.730
“We don’t know that for sure!”

00:09:01.730 --> 00:09:02.730
Polnareff carried on.

00:09:02.730 --> 00:09:03.790
“Let me go!”

00:09:03.790 --> 00:09:08.959
But Kakyoin and Joseph held onto Polnareff
tightly and continued to drag him down the

00:09:08.959 --> 00:09:13.649
passageway, hoping not to lose him to this
daytime nightmare as well.

00:09:13.649 --> 00:09:18.180
On the inside, Jotaro was shaken by the loss
of one of his companions, but nobody would

00:09:18.180 --> 00:09:21.870
have been able to tell by looking at his stoic
exterior.

00:09:21.870 --> 00:09:27.160
He was entirely focused on keeping the tunnel
expanding so that he and the remaining Crusaders

00:09:27.160 --> 00:09:29.089
could survive this ordeal together.

00:09:29.089 --> 00:09:33.860
Suddenly, a noise from the opposite end of
the passage put the group on high alert.

00:09:33.860 --> 00:09:38.410
Like a flood of liquified horror, the flesh
monsters had begun pouring themselves into

00:09:38.410 --> 00:09:42.680
the pit and were now moving towards the group
inch by inch.

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:44.940
“OH NOOOO!!!”

00:09:44.940 --> 00:09:46.290
Joseph shouted.

00:09:46.290 --> 00:09:50.600
He loosened his grip on Polnareff, and both
of them immediately booked it towards Jotaro

00:09:50.600 --> 00:09:51.600
and Iggy.

00:09:51.600 --> 00:09:54.330
Kakyoin, however, stood in place and braced
himself.

00:09:54.330 --> 00:09:57.700
He didn’t like it, but he knew what he had
to do.

00:09:57.700 --> 00:10:03.190
Right now, his stand had the ability to stop
these things, but first, he had to slow them

00:10:03.190 --> 00:10:04.190
down.

00:10:04.190 --> 00:10:05.190
“Emerald Splash!”

00:10:05.190 --> 00:10:10.019
Kakyoin shouted, prompting Hierophant Green
to launch a stream of concussive green gemstones

00:10:10.019 --> 00:10:11.450
from its hands.

00:10:11.450 --> 00:10:14.500
As planned, the attack slowed the slime monsters
down.

00:10:14.500 --> 00:10:17.750
Kakyoin was then able to put the second part
of his plan into effect.

00:10:17.750 --> 00:10:22.930
He identified what appeared to be a face on
the monster in front, and sent Hierophant

00:10:22.930 --> 00:10:26.040
Green to make its way inside the creature’s
body.

00:10:26.040 --> 00:10:31.820
This was his stand’s most terrifying ability,
and one Kakyoin seldom used: Hierophant Green

00:10:31.820 --> 00:10:36.790
had the power to control the bodies of other
physical entities from within.

00:10:36.790 --> 00:10:42.300
Once his stand had established control, Kakyoin
forced the massive ooze to stop in place,

00:10:42.300 --> 00:10:46.050
instantly plugging the tunnel and preventing
the rest of the monsters from getting any

00:10:46.050 --> 00:10:47.089
closer.

00:10:47.089 --> 00:10:51.339
How long could he keep this up, he didn’t
know, but because of Hierophant Green’s

00:10:51.339 --> 00:10:56.480
properties as a remote stand, Kakyoin was
able to run to rejoin Jotaro and the others

00:10:56.480 --> 00:10:58.020
at the front of the tunnel.

00:10:58.020 --> 00:11:02.889
The tether between himself and his stand was
stretching farther by the minute, but he dared

00:11:02.889 --> 00:11:08.079
not let his control of the oozing entity slip,
lest he and his companions suffer the same

00:11:08.079 --> 00:11:09.980
fate as Avdol.

00:11:09.980 --> 00:11:13.820
Before long, Jotaro felt a different sort
of surface at the front of the tunnel.

00:11:13.820 --> 00:11:16.190
Rather than earth, it was brick.

00:11:16.190 --> 00:11:20.950
With one punch from Star Platinum, he smashed
through and into what appeared to be an abandoned

00:11:20.950 --> 00:11:22.450
subway station.

00:11:22.450 --> 00:11:25.870
The power was still on, though most of the
lights had faded.

00:11:25.870 --> 00:11:29.339
It was fortunate that there was no natural
sunlight in this place.

00:11:29.339 --> 00:11:33.420
As everyone’s eyes adjusted to the light,
the stand users crossed the tracks and made

00:11:33.420 --> 00:11:36.730
their way onto the somewhat safer area.

00:11:36.730 --> 00:11:42.139
Polnareff drifted over to the magazine kiosk,
searching for signs of anyone behind the counter.

00:11:42.139 --> 00:11:46.790
There was nobody here, and Iggy soon helped
himself to some of the coffee-flavored chewing

00:11:46.790 --> 00:11:48.870
gum at the concession stand.

00:11:48.870 --> 00:11:52.110
The dog couldn’t resist his favorite snack
after all.

00:11:52.110 --> 00:11:56.550
Jotaro stood by the tracks, as if waiting
for a train, while Kakyoin did his best to

00:11:56.550 --> 00:12:00.139
maintain his hold on the monsters further
behind them in the tunnel.

00:12:00.139 --> 00:12:05.250
With a bit of searching, Joseph found a large
portable music player designed for CDs, also

00:12:05.250 --> 00:12:07.200
known as a boom box.

00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:11.959
With the use of his divination-focused stand,
Hermit Purple, Joseph created purple thorny

00:12:11.959 --> 00:12:17.950
vines which weaved their way into the wires
of the device and generated a psychic message.

00:12:17.950 --> 00:12:22.680
Hermit Purple could usually be counted on
to provide more detail about a situation,

00:12:22.680 --> 00:12:26.770
but its powers were limited by the device
used to gain the information.

00:12:26.770 --> 00:12:32.110
In this case, the CD within the boom box had
a copy of The Beatles’ famous 1969 album

00:12:32.110 --> 00:12:37.910
Abbey Road, so Hermit Purple’s message to
Joseph came out as a garbled but oddly appropriate

00:12:37.910 --> 00:12:42.370
rearrangement of the lyrics to Here Comes
The Sun.

00:12:42.370 --> 00:12:48.459
Little darlin’, I see their faces slowly
melting

00:12:48.459 --> 00:12:54.949
Little darlin’, it seems like years since
it’s been alright

00:12:54.949 --> 00:13:02.980
Here comes the sun
Here comes the sun, and I say

00:13:02.980 --> 00:13:10.670
I feel I been slowly melting
Sun, Sun, Sun, Here it comes

00:13:10.670 --> 00:13:14.970
“Oh my god,” Joseph said to himself quietly.

00:13:14.970 --> 00:13:19.339
Just then, Kakyoin felt the body that Hierophant
Green was controlling give way.

00:13:19.339 --> 00:13:23.449
Apparently, the pressure of so many other
ooze monsters had been too much for it to

00:13:23.449 --> 00:13:28.670
hold back, and now these things were barreling
down the tunnel towards the Crusaders.

00:13:28.670 --> 00:13:32.640
Rather than pulling Hierophant Green back
completely, Kakyoin unleashed his emerald

00:13:32.640 --> 00:13:36.630
splash over and over again in an attempt to
force a cave in.

00:13:36.630 --> 00:13:40.910
But the creatures were too resilient, and
their ooze-like structure meant they could

00:13:40.910 --> 00:13:43.329
squeeze past mere rocks in their path.

00:13:43.329 --> 00:13:48.389
Kakyoin told the rest of the group that it
was time to leave, and as if on cue, a train

00:13:48.389 --> 00:13:50.590
began to pull into the station.

00:13:50.590 --> 00:13:55.160
Unfortunately, the crazy train pulled into
the station with several cars full of ooze

00:13:55.160 --> 00:13:59.820
zombies ready to grab the poor team and drag
them into the sun.

00:13:59.820 --> 00:14:02.730
There was no way out but up the stairs.

00:14:02.730 --> 00:14:07.320
Back into the sunlight they had done everything
possible to escape.

00:14:07.320 --> 00:14:11.800
As Polnareff, Jotaro, Joseph, and Iggy did
their best to fend off the attacking creatures

00:14:11.800 --> 00:14:17.430
using their stands, Kakyoin made one last
ditch attempt to contain the monsters.

00:14:17.430 --> 00:14:22.759
He stretched Hierophant Green down to its
most basic form, a series of long green fibrous

00:14:22.759 --> 00:14:26.399
strings and created a net to ensnare the creatures.

00:14:26.399 --> 00:14:31.680
While the oozes could still seep through this
wiry form, Kakyoin rigged his stand to set

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:37.500
off an emerald splash on every bit of anomalous
goo that made it past the nets defenses.

00:14:37.500 --> 00:14:42.839
It was a sustainable and effective wall against
the monsters, using both the tensile strength

00:14:42.839 --> 00:14:47.970
of the stand and its energy attacks to effectively
stymie their progress.

00:14:47.970 --> 00:14:50.120
There was only one problem.

00:14:50.120 --> 00:14:54.330
In order to maintain this perfect defense,
Kakyoin would have to stay behind.

00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:55.470
“I’ll hold them.

00:14:55.470 --> 00:14:57.000
Go on without me!”

00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:58.639
Kakyoin said.

00:14:58.639 --> 00:14:59.800
“KAKYOIN!!”

00:14:59.800 --> 00:15:04.310
Joseph shouted, as the rest of them ran as
fast as they could out of the subway.

00:15:04.310 --> 00:15:08.490
Having effectively lost two members of the
group, The Stardust Crusaders were in low

00:15:08.490 --> 00:15:09.830
spirits.

00:15:09.830 --> 00:15:13.730
Looking up through the subway exit, they could
see that they would soon be in contact with

00:15:13.730 --> 00:15:17.690
the sunlight, meaning that even their survival
would become unlikely.

00:15:17.690 --> 00:15:20.310
But Jotaro wasn’t about to give in.

00:15:20.310 --> 00:15:23.649
He grabbed Iggy and held the dog out in front
of him.

00:15:23.649 --> 00:15:26.200
“Alright, Iggy, it’s now or never.

00:15:26.200 --> 00:15:30.040
Either show us you can be a team player or
be the first to turn into one of those blob

00:15:30.040 --> 00:15:31.040
monsters.”

00:15:31.040 --> 00:15:33.890
Iggy struggled in Jotaro’s grip, but to
no avail.

00:15:33.890 --> 00:15:39.000
The dog knew that Jotaro was serious, so in
an act of self-preservation that was usually

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:44.920
generous of him, Iggy used The Fool to stir
up the sand on the ground above into a gigantic

00:15:44.920 --> 00:15:46.670
shady sand dome.

00:15:46.670 --> 00:15:50.790
Moments later, he compressed it into a compact
fortress of sand.

00:15:50.790 --> 00:15:53.660
Iggy’s moving castle, as it were.

00:15:53.660 --> 00:15:58.720
No light could enter this fortress, but because
of the granular nature of sand, oxygen was

00:15:58.720 --> 00:16:00.160
flowing freely.

00:16:00.160 --> 00:16:06.269
The Stardust Crusaders now had a method of
travel in this world torn apart by SCP-001.

00:16:06.269 --> 00:16:10.680
Of course, there was still the matter of dealing
with the flesh creatures outside.

00:16:10.680 --> 00:16:15.070
Even if the fortress of sand could move across
the surface without sunlight getting in, the

00:16:15.070 --> 00:16:18.569
surrounding oozes could still impede its progress.

00:16:18.569 --> 00:16:24.200
With the help of all three of Jotaro, Joseph,
and Polnareff stands, a solution soon became

00:16:24.200 --> 00:16:25.200
clear.

00:16:25.200 --> 00:16:29.240
Joseph would use Hermit Purple on the sand
to divine the location of any approaching

00:16:29.240 --> 00:16:33.930
threats, while Jotaro and Polnareff would
patrol the outside of the miniaturized fortress

00:16:33.930 --> 00:16:37.529
with Star Platinum and Silver Chariot, respectively.

00:16:37.529 --> 00:16:42.390
That way, whenever a flesh creature got too
close, the two attack-type stands could unleash

00:16:42.390 --> 00:16:45.370
full-force barrages to knock them away.

00:16:45.370 --> 00:16:49.810
The next thing to do was for Iggy to increase
the speed of the sand construct by adding

00:16:49.810 --> 00:16:50.810
wheels to it.

00:16:50.810 --> 00:16:56.310
It was like a giant sand monster truck zooming
through the ruins, with a platinum brawler

00:16:56.310 --> 00:17:00.350
and a silver knight repelling anything that
came too near.

00:17:00.350 --> 00:17:04.699
Once Iggy gained enough velocity with The
Fool, Joseph used Hermit Purple to discern

00:17:04.699 --> 00:17:08.339
the location of a bit of rubble shaped conveniently
like a ramp.

00:17:08.339 --> 00:17:12.970
The sandcastle vaulted off the ramp and into
the air where Iggy augmented his creation

00:17:12.970 --> 00:17:16.370
once again with a pair of gigantic gliding
wings.

00:17:16.370 --> 00:17:18.620
Now they were soaring.

00:17:18.620 --> 00:17:23.160
Out of the reach of the flesh monsters, Joseph
and Polnareff shared sympathies over the loss

00:17:23.160 --> 00:17:25.180
of their two important friends.

00:17:25.180 --> 00:17:30.580
Avdol and Kakyoin had both bravely given themselves
to protect the team, and none of the Crusaders

00:17:30.580 --> 00:17:33.290
would be here if it wasn’t for them.

00:17:33.290 --> 00:17:38.150
Jotaro focused on helping Iggy pilot the sand-glider,
using Star Platinum to kick the ground whenever

00:17:38.150 --> 00:17:40.220
the vehicle got too low.

00:17:40.220 --> 00:17:44.770
Nobody was sure what they would encounter
next in the daybreak, or what bizarre adventures

00:17:44.770 --> 00:17:50.679
were yet to unfold, but they had each other
and for now, that was enough.

00:17:50.679 --> 00:17:55.680
Now go check out “I Survived 100 Days of
SCP-001 When Day Breaks...

00:17:55.680 --> 00:18:01.080
Here's What Happened” and “SCP-001 When
Day Breaks Tale (Hour by Hour)” for more

00:18:01.080 --> 00:18:03.160
horrifying When Day Breaks action!

